Pixel-precise (smooth) scrolling for GhosttyKit (libghostty-spm patch 0023)

Drop into libghostty-spm's Patches/ghostty/ after 0022; build.sh applies it
with `git apply`. Cut against the tree with 0001-0022 applied, Ghostty 042b16b6.

Model: the viewport keeps scrolling by whole rows; the remainder of a
precision scroll becomes a fraction in [0, cell height) by which the grid is
drawn higher, and one overscan row below the viewport (RenderState
overscan_request, upstream #14400) fills the bottom edge. Same shape as the
closed upstream PR #14210 (content_offset), driven from Surface instead of a
terminal option.

  - Surface.zig: precision scrolls in the normal (non-mouse-reporting, primary
    screen) path go to smoothScrollViewport. The fraction lives in
    renderer.State (scroll_frac_px + the scrollbar offset it belongs to); it is
    zero at the top of the scrollback and on the active area, and the renderer
    ignores it as soon as the viewport moved for any other reason.
    Discrete wheel scrolls, mouse reporting and alternate scroll are unchanged.
  - renderer: content_offset uniform (y = overscroll - fraction) applied to
    cell backgrounds, glyphs/decorations/cursor and Kitty images; while it is
    not zero, text and images are discarded outside the viewport and the
    background keeps the unshifted padding behavior. viewport_rows uniform
    (Metal) tells the viewport from the overscan row.
  - ghostty_surface_set_overscroll(surface, px): host-driven overscroll for
    rubber-banding, the uncovered strip shows the background.
  - OpenGL/GLSL: content_offset added and applied (no clipping), untested.

Measurements: docs/ghostty-eval/measure-build-consistency.md (0023 section).

